    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0446" n="1180" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1180"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Muruaga.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-03"><hi rendition="#italic">April 3,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 20th ultimo, addressed to Mr. Uhl as Acting Secretary,
                    communicating copy of a telegram from the Governor-General of Cuba in regard to
                    an alleged statement of “sailors” touching an entry in the log book of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Conde Venadito</hi>, relative to firing upon a vessel
                    said to have shown the British flag off Cape Maysi on the 8th instant, which
                    vessel the Governor-General supposes to have been the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Alliança</hi>.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
